Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:03.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I was born and raised in Harar.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.31,0:00:06.39,Default,,0,0,0,,All my childhood\Nmemories began there.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.60,0:00:10.87,Default,,0,0,0,,About 2.5 kilometers from\Nmy childhood home stood
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.87,0:00:14.08,Default,,0,0,0,,the Ras Makonnen Monument\Nat a large roundabout.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.50,0:00:19.37,Default,,0,0,0,,As a child, passing that\Nmonument often meant my parents
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.37,0:00:23.38,Default,,0,0,0,,were buying me new clothes or\Ntaking me somewhere special.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.10,0:00:26.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Those were unforgettable\Nfamily outings.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.60,0:00:30.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Seeing the monument always filled\Nme with happiness and excitement.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.80,0:00:36.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Years passed, and I grew up and\Nleft Harar to attend university.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.10,0:00:41.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I spent around five years\Nin Adama and Addis Ababa,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.64,0:00:44.62,Default,,0,0,0,,continuing my studies\Nfar from my hometown.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.60,0:00:48.42,Default,,0,0,0,,When I returned to\NHarar years later,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.42,0:00:52.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I expected to see all the\Nfamiliar places again.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.10,0:00:56.22,Default,,0,0,0,,But when I saw that the\Nmonument had been demolished,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.22,0:00:58.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I felt deeply\Ndisappointed and sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.28,0:01:01.23,Default,,0,0,0,,A familiar part of my\Nchildhood memories was gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.00,0:01:04.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Even though I was\Nback in my hometown,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.31,0:01:07.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Harar felt different from\Nthe place I remembered.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.28,0:01:11.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Familiar places hold our memories\Nand become part of who we are.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.10,0:01:15.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Heritage is not only\Nabout physical monuments;
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.30,0:01:19.68,Default,,0,0,0,,it is also about the memories and\Nemotions we attach to places.
